    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both of its tests pass. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe feature: when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners` without a `registrationDate`, the server now defaults it to today's date; when supplied it's preserved. The field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format from `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. It flows into the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and, via `allOf`, `OwnerDto` (response). `format: date` generates a `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 exactly what the test asserts. It's left out of the `required` list so it's optional on input.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column (mirroring `Pet.birthDate`), plus getter/setter.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after MapStruct maps the DTO to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when null. MapStruct copies a supplied date through by name, so client-provided dates are preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed uses positional inserts, so appended a trailing `NULL` for the new column to each of the 10 owner rows (the other dialects use column-list inserts and needed no data change).\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 both `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` pass; `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nI did not touch the PUT path (`ApplyOwner`) since the spec and tests concern creation only and no test covers editing the registration date.",
